Subject: [Krypton] Opt in to on-device Live Caption support and its native-menu command

Helium returns false from IsLiveCaptionFeatureSupported and removes one page
menu entry. Keep that behavior unless the default-off startup choice is on;
then restore supported on-device captioning and just its context-menu command.
The caption window anchors to the page's native widget, not the absent toolbar.
The shared component allowlist enables only the engine and its enumerated
language packs while this choice is on. The component endpoint uses this
choice as consent for these downloads. Small-expert models, translation and
other account-backed features remain disabled by the existing upstream patches.
Turning the switch off preserves Helium's support/menu behavior after restart.

